From d8aa323bd2b8a725884b67e040c285ce26a1d445 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pbnjlabs <328119985+pbnjlabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:24:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Add CPU fan curve, power limits and
 CFR menu

Without a Super I/O config, nct6687d_hwm_init() writes "disabled" to
every EC temperature source slot and locks them. The CPU fan channel
(EC FAN2) keeps following slot 0 and falls back to the default duty
(~30%), whatever the CPU temperature.

- Use PECI as sensor slot 0 and run FAN2 (TACH pin 10, PWM pin 9) in
  Smart Fan IV mode, with full speed at 95 C or on a sensor error.
- Add a CFR setup menu: Hyper-Threading, power on after failure,
  PL1/PL2 and a CPU fan profile (Balanced/Quiet/Performance/Full speed).
- Default PL1/PL2 to 35/45 W. An i9-9900 at 65/65 W cut power within
  ~30 s of an all-thread load on an M920x.
- superio/nuvoton/nct6687d: clear EC-default algorithm features
  (DTS, smart tracking, ambient floor, ...) that the devicetree did not
  request, keeping FAN_ALG_FUNCTRL_ALG_EN. Left on, they made the fan
  surge between ~1500 and ~6200 RPM.

TEST=M920x, i9-9900: fan follows CPU temperature under 4- and
16-thread load, peak 74-77 C, no power loss.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
